    "name": "Manège militaire Voltigeurs de Québec",
    "notes": "Manège militaire des Voltigeurs de Québec (Eugène-Étienne Taché, 1887; rebuilt after the 2008 fire, reopened 2018), Grande Allée: the stone drill hall under a steep slate roof, the château-style head building with turrets at its north-east end towards Place George-V, and the new low annex on the Plains side. Heights from the lidar survey: the hall's eaves 12.5 m and ridge 23 m, the head 25 m, the annex 6 m. Façade frame along Grande Allée, south-west to north-east.",
